course: dictionary
lesson: 4857
title: Hyrax: a word from the rocks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may not know the word hyrax, but the words around it leave clues. «The rock hyrax from the Leopard's story looks like a big guinea pig, yet its closest living relatives are elephants and manatees.» A guinea pig is small and furry, so a hyrax must be a small furry animal too.
explain: Look at more clues. The word «rock» in «rock hyrax» tells you it lives on rocks. The dictionary adds that it eats plants and lives among rocks or in trees. Always ask: what would fit here? An animal that eats plants and lives on rocks fits better than a bird or a fish.
explain: Watch for the word «yet». It shows something surprising is coming. The hyrax looks like a rodent, but «yet» tells you its closest relatives are much bigger animals, the elephants. Clue words like «yet», «but» and «although» often signal a twist.
fact: A hyrax is a small furry plant-eating mammal.
fact: Hyraxes live in Africa and the Middle East, among rocks or in trees.
fact: A hyrax looks like a big guinea pig or rabbit, but it has no long ears.
fact: Other names for the hyrax are «rock hyrax», «dassie» (South Africa) and «coney» (in the Bible).
fact: Scientists find that its closest living relatives are elephants and sea cows (manatees), shown by its teeth, feet and DNA.
exercise: What is a hyrax? | A kind of rock | *A small furry plant-eating mammal | A fish that lives in the sea | A large bird that cannot fly
exercise: «It looks like a big guinea pig, but it has no long ears.» Which animal does the hyrax look like? | A camel | *A big guinea pig or rabbit | An elephant | A snake
exercise: In South Africa, the hyrax is called a what? | Manatee | Quagga | *Dassie | Coney
test: Where does a hyrax live? | *Among rocks or in trees | Under the sea | In the deep ocean | On the Arctic ice
test: «Although it looks like a rodent, the hyrax is surprisingly related to which animal?» | The mouse | *The elephant | The owl | The lion
exam: Hyraxes eat plants, so they are called what kind of eaters? | Insect-eaters | Fish-eaters | Meat-eaters | *Plant-eaters
